Hybrid CPU dequant for large frames — PUNKTFUNK LOCAL PATCH.

Not upstream.

WHY. With 0014 the G52 still needs 20-24 ms of GPU time per 4K frame at 300 Mbps (live: about
50 fps), over the 16.7 ms a 60 fps stream allows. Every further shader change got close but not
under, because the iDWT alone is at the GPU's memory bandwidth.

WHAT IT DOES. Adds cpudq.hpp: the dequant (bitplane unpacking into wavelet coefficients) runs on
the CPU with NEON FP16 across several threads, writing linear write-combined images the GPU reads
directly, and the GPU only runs the iDWT, one frame behind. Enabled by PYROWAVE_CPU_DEQUANT=1
(PYROWAVE_CPU_DEQUANT_NICE sets the threads' priority); the webOS client sets it above 1080p.
Granite gains map/unmap for image memory and lets linear array images skip device-local memory.
On an LG C5, 4K60 at 300 Mbps holds 60 fps with about 17 ms of GPU time.

